  "releaseNotes": "1.0.4: Android multicast reception. New AndroidMulticastSupport helper (ref-counted WifiManager.MulticastLock) so consumers can hold the lock for the lifetime of SSDP activity — without it, Android's WiFi driver filters incoming multicast even when CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE is granted. SsdpDevicePublisher on Android now acquires the lock in its constructor and releases on Dispose. Locator consumers should call AndroidMulticastSupport.Acquire(tag) from their app's Android initialization (e.g. MainApplication.OnCreate). Requires ACCESS_WIFI_STATE + CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE permissions in the app manifest. 1.0.3: iOS multicast reception fix. Multicast listener now binds to INADDR_ANY while still joining IGMP on the configured local interface. Receive loop also reconnects on generic socket exceptions and distinguishes broadcast vs send socket for reconnect targeting.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "verbatimVersion": "1.0.4",
